A1. What is a wise-cracker? ~ JOKER
A5. What do you have to do since prohibition to get a drink? ~ ASK
A7. What is found under the hood? ~ MOTOR
A11. Name an exclamation of delight. ~ AH
A12. What is the most breakable thing you know? ~ LAW
A14. Name a listening-in device. ~ EAR
A15. Name a note in the scale. ~ FA
A16. What is a beastly thing to study? ~ ZOOLOGY
A17. Name a convenient expression of faltering alibi artists. ~ ER
A19. What is often used in a pinch? ~ COP
A20. Name something often at sea. ~ GOB
A22. Name a favorite little pronoun. ~ ME
A23. What is sweet enough to eat? ~ SUGAR
A25. Name a conjunction. ~ AND
A27. What has no noses—but smells nicely nevertheless? ~ ROSES
A29. Who is a well-known silent pardner? ~ DAD
A30. Where is junk usually stored? ~ ATTIC
A32. What verb means "to affect with pain or uneasiness"? ~ AIL
A33. What is easier to break into than out of? ~ PEN
A34. Name a part of the verb "to be." ~ ARE
A35. What kind of senators are "all wet"? ~ DRY
A37. In what should road hogs be put? ~ STY
A39. What do snow birds eat? ~ DOPE
A40. Where is the Orient? ~ EAST
A41. Where do golf champions get their start? ~ TEE
A43. What is the finish of anything? ~ END
A45. What is a hot dogma? ~ ISM
A46. What animal inhabits crossword puzzles? ~ EMU
A48. What do few artists do for a living? ~ ART
A50. What goes faster when tired—than not? (plural). ~ AUTOS
A52. Name something unrefined. ~ ORE
A53. Name a playful pastime of anarchists. ~ ARSON
A55. What is a proclamation of marriage? ~ BAN
A56. What is a proof of Uncle Sam's metal? ~ ASSAY
A58. Where can you stay—if you don't want to be found out? ~ IN
A59. What are most dry agents? ~ WET
A61. Give the nickname of a famous President. ~ ABE
A62. What exclamation means the same as "lookit"? ~ LO
A63. What did Jack Dempsey and Jack Sharkey have between them? ~ RIVALRY
A64. Name a French conjunction. ~ ET
A66. Who was Adam's side-kick? ~ EVE
A67. What is usually rejected? (abbr.) ~ MSS
A69. Name an indefinite article. ~ AN
A70. What can be seen but not heard? ~ DUMMY
A71. What are raised in the wide-open spaces? ~ MEN
A72. Name a novel written by Edna Ferber (two words). ~ SOBIG

D1. How does 10th Avenue designate "the ladies"? ~ JANES
D2. Name an exclamation of surprise. ~ OH
D3. What is an overhead railroad called? ~ EL
D4. What can Rastus hold that would beat a royal flush? ~ RAZOR
D6. What would Dora be if she were really dumb? ~ SILENT
D7. Who puts on the high hat in New York when distinguished visitors come? ~ MAYOR
D8. Name a little conjunction. ~ OR
D9. Name a little preposition. ~ OF
D10. Where do people get a run for their money? ~ RACES
D13. What do Mussolini's enemies call him? ~ WOP
D14. Name something often hard-boiled. ~ EGG
D18. What is the traffic cop to the wayward motorist? ~ RUDE
D19. Name a term of contempt. ~ CAD
D21. What do flappers like for a neck? ~ BOA
D22. What does a diamond ring do to many an icy disposition? ~ MELT
D24. What is often found around a silly little goose? ~ GANDERS
D25. What did the motorist do at the filling station? ~ ATE
D26. What is the past tense of a word meaning "to achieve"? ~ DID
D28. What do small boys have very little use for? ~ SISTERS
D30. Where is the bull often thrown? ~ ARENA
D31. Name a specie of plant used in salad. ~ CRESS
D33. [no clue printed] ~ PET
D34. Name something noted for its monkeyshines. ~ APE
D36. What is the sweet potato of the tropics? ~ YAM
D38. Name a pronoun. ~ YOU
D42. Name an antiquated way to get money. ~ EARN
D44. What kind of person is usually boastful? ~ DUB
D45. What substance results from electrolytic decomposition? ~ ION
D47. What do most people eat at dinner time? ~ MEAL
D49. Name something that has a lot of pull. ~ TOW
D51. What is hot stuff in Mexico? ~ TAMALE
D52. Name a suffix used to indicate fulness or abundance. ~ OSE
D53. What did the Rev. Straton do with his views on Evolution? ~ AIZED
D54. What kind of person is Chas. A. Lindbergh? ~ NERVY
D56. Name something that always seems to be yawning. ~ ABYSS
D57. What is impossible for even the most successful people to be very long? ~ YOUNG
D60. What do preachers do to the bonds of matrimony? ~ TIE
D61. What is often seen around the waist spaces? ~ ARM
D65. What was one of Cæsar's last words? ~ TU
D66. Name a printer's measure. ~ EM
D68. Name an adverb which means "in this or that manner." ~ SO
D69. Name a three-toed sloth. ~ AI


